    "created_at": "2026-09-30T19:23:36Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-09-30T19:23:36Z",
    "body": "There are instances where binary estimators can't produce an estimate but where the result is not an error; in such instances the estimator returns exactly 1, which cannot impact the final result. This is not an error, and should not be flagged as one. A sub-1000000 sample input should probably be treated as an error. The other identified instances shouldn't occur if this sample size is enforced.",
