    "created_at": "2026-09-30T23:20:32Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-09-30T23:20:32Z",
    "body": "Thanks — that distinction makes sense. I'll narrow this accordingly: sub-1,000,000-sample input should be treated as an error, while a legitimate estimator no-result/full-entropy sentinel that cannot affect the final minimum should not automatically be classified as an assessment error.\n",
